    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i'm also seeing a lot of people saying that the universal museum model is basically an outdated, colonialist way of looking at things and that it's basically impossible for a museum to be truly \"neutral\" if it keeps these items. do you think it's even possible to defend the universalist view anymore without sounding like you're ignoring the moral reality of the situation?",
