      "content": "Defending the universalist view today requires a significant pivot toward rigorous ethical accountability rather than just curatorial prestige. Instead of claiming neutrality, proponents must argue for a commitment to \"stewardship\" and continuous re-evaluation of provenance, acknowledging the historical power imbalances. A strong defense would emphasize collaboration, decolonization of interpretation, and creating pathways for shared custodianship, rather than absolute retention. This shifts the focus from *control* to *responsibility*.",
      "source": "target",
